<title>USA: Union takes another swipe at Unocal on Burma.</title>
<headline>Union takes another swipe at Unocal on Burma.</headline>
<dateline>LAKEWOOD, Colo 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Oil, Chemical and Atomic Workers International Union (OCAW) on Thursday stepped up its campaign to get Unocal Corp to exit Burma with a letter to four non-executive board members.</p>
<p>OCAW president Robert Wages told the four that &quot;anything short of Unocal pulling out of Burma should prompt you to resign from Unocal's board.&quot;</p>
<p>The union alleges that Unocal's involvement in Burma gives that country's military regime succor and financial support.</p>
<p>Unocal says that its role in Burma's economy is positive, that it provides employment at above-average wages, education and training and health programmes. ((-- New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
